{% set local_problems %}
<p>Triana is one of the oldest towns in Alabama — and one of the wettest. Sitting directly on the Tennessee River in southwest Madison County, this historic community deals with water from every direction. The river keeps the water table high, humidity stays elevated year-round, and when heavy rains hit, properties here face drainage challenges that inland homes never see.</p>

<p>Standard gutter systems that work fine in Huntsville often aren't adequate for Triana. The combination of high groundwater, river humidity, and intense seasonal rainfall means homes here need gutters that can move water quickly and route it far from foundations that are already under pressure from below.</p>

<p>Many Triana homes are also historic, with the character and charm that comes from nearly two centuries of history — but also with drainage systems that need updating for modern conditions.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_local %}
<p>We understand river communities. Triana's challenges are similar to what we see in parts of Decatur — high water tables, humidity effects on materials, and the need for drainage solutions that go beyond standard suburban installations. We're just 15 miles away, and we've been serving southwest Madison County for over two decades.</p>
{% endset %}
